      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 5,000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day, nearly four times the usual adult maximum of 4 g/day. A dose like that risks serious hepatotoxicity and acute liver failure. A single 5,000 mg dose is also well above the typical 500\u20131,000 mg per dose.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **500 mg PO three times daily** (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2.6 g/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily** (3 g/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO four times daily** (4 g/day, the maximum, and often limited to 3 g/day for prolonged use)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. Please also confirm the plan with your supervising resident or attending. If 5,000 mg was intentional, for example if the number was meant to be a total daily dose, let me know that too."
      }
