    "type": "assistant",
    "message": {
     "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
     "id": "msg_011Ch3G7co2aYYqcvkaFMPs6",
     "type": "message",
     "role": "assistant",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 15 g/day of acetaminophen is a potentially lethal dose. For a 70 kg adult, a single 5,000 mg dose is about 71 mg/kg, which is below the acute toxicity threshold of roughly 150 mg/kg but still far above any safe therapeutic dose. Repeating it three times daily would very likely cause severe liver injury. Normal liver and kidney function and no allergies don't change that.\n\nYou can still get the order placed safely:\n- **If the dose was a mistake**, give me the dose and frequency you want. Examples are 1,000 mg PO every 8 hours or 650 mg PO every 6 hours, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **If you think this is clinically intended**, talk to your attending or the pharmacist first. An order like this would need to go through them and not be placed by a student.\n- **If you're worried about an overdose or an ingestion**, contact poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) or toxicology now. N-acetylcysteine treatment is a separate order and not something to cover with a scheduled acetaminophen dose.\n\nI can enter a corrected order as soon as you tell me what you'd like."
      }
     ],
